  "permutation_floor_caveat": "With only n_t=4 (or fewer, per-ROI) subjects contributing valid held-out templates, the subject-respecting permutation null has only 4! = 24 distinct label arrangements; even with N_PERM=5000 resamples the achievable minimum empirical p-value is bounded near 1/24 = 0.042 for every ROI simultaneously. This is why the independent fMRI-derived permutation p-values cluster tightly around 0.03-0.05 and *all* clear an uncorrected/BH threshold (25/25 'survive' BH-FDR here) while *none* clear Bonferroni (0/25) -- consistent in direction with the committed analysis's 0/25 Bonferroni-survivors, but the BH result here should NOT be read as 25 independently robust ROI effects: it is an artifact of a permutation null with a hard p-floor at N=4, which BH-FDR does not protect against when nearly all p-values sit at that floor. Bonferroni (or exact combinatorial testing, or a larger N) is the only trustworthy correction under N=4.",
